[05:02:30] [Server thread/INFO]: Add Command Help
Create waypoint lists or add waypoints with quick defaults or full properties.
Usage
  /wp add <dimension> <list-identifier> - Create an empty waypoint list in the selected dimension
  /wp add <position> <list-identifier> <waypoint-identifier> - Quickly add a waypoint in your current dimension using automatic properties
  /wp add <position> <list-identifier> <waypoint-identifier> <initials> <color> <yaw> <global> [<keywords> [<description>]] - Add a waypoint with every property in your current dimension
  /wp add <dimension> <list-identifier> <position> <waypoint-identifier> <initials> <color> <yaw> <global> [<keywords> [<description>]] - Add a waypoint with every property in a selected dimension
Arguments
  <dimension> - A dimension ID such as minecraft:overworld
  <position> - Absolute or relative block coordinates, such as 100 64 -20 or ~ ~ ~
  <list-identifier> / <waypoint-identifier> - Exact identifiers used for lookup; they are never parsed as display text, and Brigadier-sensitive values must be quoted
  <initials> - The short label displayed for the waypoint; quote it if it contains spaces
  <color> - A vanilla color name, six-digit RGB hex code, or random; hover the autocomplete suggestion to preview the color of your hex input
  <yaw> - An integer facing direction in degrees
  <global> - true for global visibility; false for local visibility
  <keywords> - Optional comma-separated plain-text search terms; quote the group when it contains spaces
  <description> - Optional plain text or Minecraft JSON text shown to players; requires the keywords argument first (use an empty string for none)
Examples
  /wp add minecraft:overworld "Home Bases" - Create the Home Bases list in the Overworld
  /wp add ~ ~ ~ "Home Bases" "Main Home" - Quickly add Main Home at your current position
  /wp add minecraft:overworld "Home Bases" ~ ~ ~ "Main Home" MH gold 0 true - Add Main Home with explicitly selected properties
[←] Back to main help
